  "instructions": [
    "Heat olive oil in a large pot over medium heat.",
    "Add onion, garlic, carrot, and celery, sauté until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Stir in canned tomatoes, vegetable broth, water, and shio-koji, bringing to a simmer.",
    "Reduce heat to low and let the soup simmer gently for 15 minutes to meld flavors.",
    "Use an immersion blender to aerate the soup until silky but not fully smooth, leaving some texture.",
    "Season with lemon juice, pepper, and a pinch of salt if needed, adjusting for taste.",
    "Ladle the soup into bowls and sprinkle fresh basil leaves over the top.",
    "Serve hot, optionally with a drizzle of olive oil."
